 "differences": [
  "The paper gives the total as 97,350 records and also says 'over 90,000 strokes'; the deposit has 97,350 rows, which match the first number.",
  "The paper's text calls mode 1 both 'aerobic swing' and 'full power stroke' and ties the three serving-machine ball speeds to different modes in different places; the deposit README (mode 0 air swing, 1 full power stroke, 2 stable hitting) and the data (stages 1-3 occur only in mode 1) agree, and are used here.",
  "50 rows of the deposit are exact duplicates of another row; all rows are kept as shared. The 'fileindex' (here 'round') is not unique within a player, mode and stage: some combinations hold 100 or 150 strokes (two or three rounds on different dates), so use date as well.",
  "Age, experience, height and weight are only given as low/medium/high tiers (privacy), so age is empty and the tiers are in participants.csv.",
  "The Dryad record states CC0 and the Zenodo copy used here states Apache-2.0; both allow sharing a converted copy."
